For what you pay me, right?

310
00:18:40,125 --> 00:18:42,958
Yeah, right, and I bet you make more off
your business ventures, right?

311
00:18:43,041 --> 00:18:45,000
Oh, well, yeah. So I'm not broke. Look.

312
00:18:45,083 --> 00:18:46,875
A businessman, an entrepreneur
who steals auto parts!

313
00:18:46,958 --> 00:18:48,666
Hey! Shut up!

314
00:18:49,166 --> 00:18:50,083
Shut up.

315
00:18:56,458 --> 00:18:58,958
Look, if you're not afraid
of honest work,

316
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,041
we'll head out tomorrow afternoon.

317
00:19:09,666 --> 00:19:13,125
Forgive him, Candi.
You know how proud he is.

318
00:19:13,208 --> 00:19:17,000
But please, if you don't want to do it
for your brother,

319
00:19:17,666 --> 00:19:19,583
do it for yourself and your mom.

320
00:19:21,583 --> 00:19:22,625
Okay, kiddo.

321
00:19:42,666 --> 00:19:45,333
7 HOURS BEFORE THE HURRICANE

322
00:19:49,875 --> 00:19:51,500
You sure you don't want a sandwich?

323
00:19:51,583 --> 00:19:52,875
No, Mom. I have to go now.

324
00:19:52,958 --> 00:19:54,291
Please take good care of yourself.

325
00:19:54,375 --> 00:19:56,541
stay away from the water
and bundle up, okay?

326
00:19:56,625 --> 00:19:59,333
Okay, Mom. Don't worry, it's just a storm.

327
00:19:59,958 --> 00:20:01,375
It'll be mild, I'm sure.

328
00:20:01,458 --> 00:20:03,125
You'll catch a cold.

329
00:20:03,208 --> 00:20:06,208
Your immune system is weak,
you're not eating, and you're so skinny.

330
00:20:06,291 --> 00:20:09,666
Everything's going to be fine.
I've kept vigil before.

331
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:11,583
Yeah, son, but never as captain.

332
00:20:11,666 --> 00:20:14,041
And a captain
never abandons his ship, Mom.

333
00:20:18,583 --> 00:20:19,583
Just kidding.

334
00:20:25,208 --> 00:20:27,208
Of course he wasn't going to come.

335
00:20:27,291 --> 00:20:28,833
It's Candi, what did you expect?

336
00:20:28,916 --> 00:20:30,958
Well, that he wouldn't leave you alone.

337
00:20:31,041 --> 00:20:33,541
I won't be alone.
Once I've got the money in my pocket,

338
00:20:33,625 --> 00:20:35,666
I'll snag a sailor from the dock.

339
00:20:36,458 --> 00:20:37,750
Relax, Mom.

340
00:20:46,708 --> 00:20:48,375
See you in the morning, Mom.

341
00:20:49,625 --> 00:20:50,541
Bye, Mochis.

342
00:20:54,375 --> 00:20:55,250
Wirpul!

343
00:20:57,416 --> 00:20:58,333
Goodbye, Mom.

344
00:21:06,333 --> 00:21:07,833
Mochis, come here.

345
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:10,375
Come on, help me with the food.

346
00:21:10,458 --> 00:21:11,708
Hurry up!

347
00:21:19,666 --> 00:21:20,500
Hey, dude!

348
00:21:20,583 --> 00:21:22,583
Give me eight tripe tacos to go.

349
00:21:23,458 --> 00:21:26,541
And put it on the captain's tab.

350
00:21:28,166 --> 00:21:31,041
What? Were you really going
to leave without me?

351
00:21:31,125 --> 00:21:33,208
I thought you bitched out
because of the storm.

352
00:21:33,291 --> 00:21:34,708
Dude, I was just late.

353
00:21:35,250 --> 00:21:36,208
And I haven't eaten.

354
00:21:36,291 --> 00:21:39,000
Yeah, you haven't eaten
because you're a fucking swindler.

355
00:21:39,083 --> 00:21:40,958
Stop being a fucking prude, dude.

356
00:21:42,208 --> 00:21:43,916
You have to learn to survive.

357
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,541
Survive by working, Candi.

358
00:21:46,291 --> 00:21:47,666
You need an honest job.

359
00:21:49,125 --> 00:21:52,041
And what do you think?
You think your bosses are honest?

360
00:21:52,125 --> 00:21:55,750
Stay away from the coast!

361
00:21:56,333 --> 00:21:58,708
Take care of children and the elderly!

362
00:21:58,791 --> 00:22:02,291
Otis has gone from a tropical storm
to a hurricane!

363
00:22:02,375 --> 00:22:05,041
It's approaching Acapulco!

364
00:22:05,125 --> 00:22:06,125
Did you hear that?

365
00:22:06,833 --> 00:22:09,708
Your little storm
has turned into a hurricane, man.

366
00:22:09,791 --> 00:22:11,916
Does this feel like a hurricane?

367
00:22:14,375 --> 00:22:15,625
Are you scared yet?

368
00:22:21,250 --> 00:22:23,125
Here's your pastor's order.

369
00:22:26,375 --> 00:22:29,083
With you as captain?
What could "wo grong"?

370
00:22:29,791 --> 00:22:31,333
Let's get the fuck out of here.

371
00:22:33,291 --> 00:22:34,375
Have a great meal.

372
00:22:38,541 --> 00:22:39,666
What the fuck is that?

373
00:22:39,750 --> 00:22:41,416
Are you a toddler or what?

374
00:22:41,500 --> 00:22:42,500
Go fuck yourself.

375
00:22:43,250 --> 00:22:44,083
Hey.

376
00:22:44,750 --> 00:22:46,416
Buy us some beers, will you?

377
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:48,125
Let's go to 7-Eleven.

378
00:22:48,208 --> 00:22:49,833
Your mother is a pain in the ass.

379
00:22:49,916 --> 00:22:51,583
The one who's asking for it.

380
00:22:51,666 --> 00:22:52,708
What's up, man?

381
00:22:56,916 --> 00:22:57,875
What's up, Dad?

382
00:22:58,375 --> 00:22:59,250
How are you?

383
00:22:59,333 --> 00:23:00,583
<i>Hi, what are you doing?</i>

384
00:23:00,666 --> 00:23:01,958
Just working. How about you?

385
00:23:02,041 --> 00:23:03,458
-How's Kenia?
<i>-Great.</i>

386
00:23:03,541 --> 00:23:04,666
-No, dude, wait.
-Wait.

387
00:23:04,750 --> 00:23:06,083
<i>Have you seen the news about Acapulco?</i>

388
00:23:06,166 --> 00:23:09,041
Give me a minute, chief.
I'm just coming out of a meeting.

389
00:23:09,125 --> 00:23:13,083
<i>It'll be a hurricane and they're</i>
<i>forecasting it'll reach Category 3.</i>

390
00:23:13,166 --> 00:23:15,333
<i>Is the yacht properly secured?</i>

391
00:23:15,416 --> 00:23:17,666
Yeah, I've been working on that
since yesterday.

392
00:23:17,750 --> 00:23:19,333
Kevin's taking care of it.

393
00:23:19,416 --> 00:23:23,416
<i>It's going to get really bad. You did pay</i>
<i>your yacht club dues for the year, right?</i>

394
00:23:23,500 --> 00:23:24,666
Yes, of course.

395
00:23:24,750 --> 00:23:28,250
<i>Call me in the early morning if you</i>
<i>need anything. It's almost dawn here.</i>

396
00:23:28,333 --> 00:23:29,250
Okay. Bye, Dad.

397
00:23:29,333 --> 00:23:33,833
<i>We recommend following the state</i>
<i>government's guidelines and staying home.</i>

398
00:23:40,416 --> 00:23:42,625
And how are you getting money now?

399
00:23:42,708 --> 00:23:45,041
Ah, that's really
none of your business, is it?

400
00:23:45,125 --> 00:23:46,875
It is my business, you asshole.

401
00:23:46,958 --> 00:23:48,875
Your mom just decided to sell the house.

402
00:23:48,958 --> 00:23:50,791
You idiot, she didn't just decide that.

403
00:23:50,875 --> 00:23:51,708
Man.

404
00:23:51,791 --> 00:23:54,208
It was bound to happen
once my dad was gone.

405
00:23:54,791 --> 00:23:55,833
Did you see him?

406
00:23:55,916 --> 00:23:56,875
Who?

407
00:23:57,708 --> 00:23:59,500
What do you mean, "who"? Chevo.

408
00:24:00,500 --> 00:24:01,625
Your dad, asshole.

409
00:24:01,708 --> 00:24:02,708
Chevo.

410
00:24:02,791 --> 00:24:05,500
Put the cover on the propellers
so the boat doesn't get scratched.

411
00:24:05,583 --> 00:24:06,833
Did you cover the speakers?

412
00:24:06,916 --> 00:24:09,125
They'd already taken him
by the time I got there.

413
00:24:10,916 --> 00:24:12,166
Aren't you worried?

414
00:24:14,500 --> 00:24:16,958
My dad got mugged
because he wasn't paying attention.

415
00:24:17,041 --> 00:24:19,291
You just have to stay on your toes, right?

416
00:24:19,375 --> 00:24:21,416
If you want to play dumb,
play dumb, Candi.

417
00:24:21,500 --> 00:24:23,625
Because if not, they'll fill with water…

418
00:24:23,708 --> 00:24:27,000
I just want to know that my mom and I
don't have anything to worry about.

419
00:24:27,625 --> 00:24:29,625
You know what you should be worried about,
asshole?

420
00:24:29,708 --> 00:24:32,541
That Kevin doesn't find out
you're fucking his sister.

421
00:24:32,625 --> 00:24:34,166
Who says I'm fucking his sister?

422
00:24:34,250 --> 00:24:36,833
No, well,
fucking rumors have legs, asshole.

423
00:24:37,500 --> 00:24:39,416
But look, don't worry,
if anything happens,

424
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:41,416
your big brother will defend you, asshole.

425
00:24:41,500 --> 00:24:43,166
You're not my brother, asshole.

426
00:24:43,250 --> 00:24:45,666
What? We're taking care of this shit?

427
00:24:46,166 --> 00:24:47,583
This is to get us there, idiot.

428
00:24:47,666 --> 00:24:48,708
That's the boat.

429
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:52,750
And wouldn't it be better to get her
into the yacht club?

430
00:24:52,833 --> 00:24:54,458
That's only for millionaires.

431
00:24:54,541 --> 00:24:56,958
And what do you think
your bosses are, you asshole?

432
00:24:58,625 --> 00:24:59,916
You're such an idiot.

433
00:25:00,833 --> 00:25:02,208
Here, untie the dinghy.

434
00:25:03,250 --> 00:25:04,333
What's the dinghy?

435
00:25:04,416 --> 00:25:05,958
The boat, damn it. Untie the boat!

436
00:25:06,041 --> 00:25:07,583
Well, just say "the boat," asshole.

437
00:25:15,291 --> 00:25:16,375
Don't toss it.

438
00:25:38,500 --> 00:25:39,333
Want one?

439
00:25:50,666 --> 00:25:51,916
What the heck?

440
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:54,958
Tie the dinghy to the cleat,
pass the line under the railing.

441
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:57,250
Do it today, eh?

442
00:25:57,333 --> 00:25:58,333
"Do it today."

443
00:26:02,416 --> 00:26:03,375
What's up, boss?

444
00:26:03,458 --> 00:26:05,333
<i>How are you, bro?</i>
<i>How's everything going?</i>

445
00:26:05,416 --> 00:26:07,916
All good, boss, all good.
I found a sailor.

446
00:26:08,833 --> 00:26:10,750
A top-notch mechanic.

447
00:26:10,833 --> 00:26:12,541
<i>Yeah, that's awesome.</i>

448
00:26:12,625 --> 00:26:14,333
<i>Did you guys buy your tacos?</i>

449
00:26:14,416 --> 00:26:16,166
Yeah, boss. We've got them, thanks.

450
00:26:16,250 --> 00:26:17,333
<i>-Fuck, yeah.</i>
-Yeah.

451
00:26:17,416 --> 00:26:20,208
<i>Hey, I want to tell you something,</i>
<i>but don't freak out.</i>

452
00:26:20,291 --> 00:26:24,166
<i>I think this is going to be a little</i>
<i>more complicated than we first thought.</i>

453
00:26:24,250 --> 00:26:26,291
<i>I mean, you know this boat better</i>
<i>than anyone,</i>

454
00:26:26,375 --> 00:26:28,916
<i>and it's unlikely, but just in case,</i>
<i>tie it down…</i>

455
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:30,583
-Yes.
-…<i>as tight as you can, man.</i>

456
00:26:30,666 --> 00:26:32,375
Yes, don't worry, boss.

457
00:26:32,458 --> 00:26:35,250
<i>Okay. Hey, one last thing.</i>
<i>If anything happens,</i>

458
00:26:35,333 --> 00:26:38,541
<i>you say that it was docked</i>
<i>at the yacht club. Got it?</i>

459
00:26:39,625 --> 00:26:41,208
-Yes.
<i>-All right.</i>

460
00:26:41,291 --> 00:26:42,125
Yes, boss.

461
00:26:43,083 --> 00:26:46,250
<i>Call me if you need anything.</i>
<i>I'll be keeping an eye on things here.</i>

462
00:26:46,333 --> 00:26:47,166
Sure.

463
00:26:48,791 --> 00:26:51,541
Your boss isn't just cheap,
he's a crook, that bastard.

464
00:26:51,625 --> 00:26:52,833
Shut up.

465
00:27:00,583 --> 00:27:01,500
We better go.

466
00:27:01,583 --> 00:27:03,416
No, no, this boat is my responsibility.

467
00:27:03,500 --> 00:27:05,333
-Your responsibility?
-Yes.

468
00:27:05,416 --> 00:27:06,916
Didn't you hear that asshole?

469
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:10,375
If the boat sinks, you just have to say
it broke loose from the club.

470
00:27:10,458 --> 00:27:13,333
No one has to know you weren't here
when it went to hell.

471
00:27:13,416 --> 00:27:16,916
You think anyone's going to hire me again
if I abandon my boat?

472
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:20,541
And you think they're going
to hire you again if you drown, asshole?

473
00:27:20,625 --> 00:27:23,208
Yeah, for you
everything's always so easy, Candi.

474
00:27:23,291 --> 00:27:25,916
You don't care about screwing
others over. You're just like your dad.

475
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:27,041
He's your dad too.

476
00:27:28,458 --> 00:27:32,041
That's why I have to do things right,
so they can see that I'm different.

477
00:27:32,125 --> 00:27:34,833
Yeah, you don't give a shit
about anything.

478
00:27:34,916 --> 00:27:37,083
You've never been
responsible for anything.

479
00:27:44,041 --> 00:27:44,875
No.

480
00:28:10,708 --> 00:28:12,250
Aren't you going to help me?

481
00:28:13,125 --> 00:28:16,125
My job is just to fix this thing
if it breaks down.

482
00:28:18,083 --> 00:28:20,083
Did you tie the dinghy down tight?

483
00:28:21,250 --> 00:28:22,250
I told you I did.

484
00:28:32,125 --> 00:28:33,333
Turn that off.

485
00:28:34,708 --> 00:28:35,541
No.

486
00:28:36,458 --> 00:28:38,666
And hurry up, the wind's picking up.

487
00:28:40,291 --> 00:28:42,833
Did I tell you
about that asshole I met at the Palladium?

488
00:28:42,916 --> 00:28:43,916
Which one?

489
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:47,458
The one I met when I was working
at the Palladium, kicking out drunks.

490
00:28:48,500 --> 00:28:51,541
-You used to work kicking out drunks?
-Yes.

491
00:28:52,125 --> 00:28:57,000
Well, the thing is,
one night this guy showed up.

492
00:28:57,833 --> 00:28:59,500
But you know what he looked like?

493
00:28:59,583 --> 00:29:00,416
What?

494
00:29:00,500 --> 00:29:02,500
Like he'd been abducted by aliens.

495
00:29:03,416 --> 00:29:05,083
Do you still believe in aliens?

496
00:29:05,166 --> 00:29:06,250
What? You don't?

497
00:29:07,250 --> 00:29:09,833
Real sailors always see
strange lights at sea.

498
00:29:09,916 --> 00:29:10,875
They're reflections.

499
00:29:10,958 --> 00:29:12,541
Oh, yeah, sure, reflections.

500
00:29:12,625 --> 00:29:14,166
The UFO phenomenon has been well studied.

501
00:29:15,666 --> 00:29:19,458
The thing is that this guy had that look.

502
00:29:20,875 --> 00:29:21,708
What look?

503
00:29:23,791 --> 00:29:26,916
The look of someone who's seen
something almost no one else has seen.

504
00:29:30,625 --> 00:29:31,916
Aliens, you mean.

505
00:29:35,583 --> 00:29:36,625
Death, Wirpul.

506
00:29:39,166 --> 00:29:40,791
He was a sailor like you.

507
00:29:42,625 --> 00:29:46,125
He worked in Los Cabos.
He told me he survived a hurricane.

508
00:29:46,791 --> 00:29:49,291
He had to pull his friends out with a hook

509
00:29:49,375 --> 00:29:52,000
when they were
already bloated on the beach.

510
00:29:53,500 --> 00:29:56,458
And he also told me
it had been a Category 3 hurricane.

511
00:29:58,000 --> 00:29:59,500
Maybe they weren't prepared, huh?

512
00:29:59,583 --> 00:30:01,625
Oh, fuck! And what are we prepared with?

513
00:30:01,708 --> 00:30:04,500
Oh, yeah, some tacos, some fries,
and a few beers, right?

514
00:30:06,625 --> 00:30:09,250
Have you ever been
in a Category 3 hurricane?

515
00:30:09,333 --> 00:30:10,416
Or Category 5?

516
00:30:11,166 --> 00:30:12,083
No.

517
00:30:12,166 --> 00:30:13,666
-So?
-So what?

518
00:30:15,458 --> 00:30:16,958
What time are we leaving?

519
00:30:17,041 --> 00:30:19,333
We don't know
what category is going to hit.

520
00:30:20,708 --> 00:30:23,750
And a Cat 5 hurricane never hit Acapulco.
No, it's impossible.

521
00:30:23,833 --> 00:30:24,750
Impossible?

522
00:30:25,250 --> 00:30:28,625
People say it's like
the devil's been unleashed.

523
00:30:28,708 --> 00:30:30,750
No way, Candi.
I've already been through a Category 2.

524
00:30:30,833 --> 00:30:32,166
I've been through it.

525
00:30:32,916 --> 00:30:36,375
Yeah, it's fucking awful,
but you can handle it.

526
00:30:36,458 --> 00:30:39,916
You put on your life jacket, you're ready
in case other boats crash into you.

527
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:42,916
After a while it's over, man.
It's no big deal.

528
00:30:44,750 --> 00:30:46,541
If you're scared, then leave.

529
00:30:46,625 --> 00:30:50,083
My responsibility is
to take care of this boat, that's all.

530
00:30:52,833 --> 00:30:53,666
What?

531
00:30:56,583 --> 00:30:58,375
You're just as damn stubborn as my dad.

532
00:30:58,458 --> 00:31:00,500
Responsible, like my mom.

533
00:31:00,583 --> 00:31:02,875
Oh, yeah, so responsible,
going and messing around

534
00:31:02,958 --> 00:31:04,208
with someone else's husband.

535
00:31:04,291 --> 00:31:05,708
They told me a different story.

536
00:31:05,791 --> 00:31:07,666
Yeah, asshole, I don't doubt it.

537
00:31:07,750 --> 00:31:09,541
-Son of… Only you.
<i>-This is Marlon, from </i>La Proeza.

538
00:31:09,625 --> 00:31:11,208
Majestuoso. Majestuoso.

539
00:31:25,416 --> 00:31:27,750
Majestuoso. Majestuoso, <i>do you hear me?</i>

540
00:31:28,666 --> 00:31:32,125
This is Wirpul,
from <i>El Majestuoso II. </i>Over.

541
00:31:34,041 --> 00:31:36,666
<i>What's up, my Wirpul?</i>
<i>How's my new cap doing?</i>

542
00:31:37,208 --> 00:31:38,458
<i>All smooth sailing.</i>

543
00:31:40,791 --> 00:31:43,458
Okay, turn on your lights,
let's see where you are. Over.

544
00:31:46,875 --> 00:31:47,750
I see you.

545
00:31:52,708 --> 00:31:55,750
<i>This is a message</i>
<i>from the Harbor Master's Office.</i>

546
00:31:55,833 --> 00:31:58,125
<i>All boat skippers</i>
<i>and captains are informed</i>

547
00:31:58,208 --> 00:32:00,208
<i>that navigation is closed to vessels.</i>

548
00:32:00,291 --> 00:32:04,500
<i>Hurricane Otis is forecast to intensify</i>
<i>and make landfall in the early hours.</i>

549
00:32:04,583 --> 00:32:06,916
<i>Take all necessary precautions.</i>

550
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:08,750
<i>We appreciate your acknowledgment.</i>

551
00:32:08,833 --> 00:32:10,250
<i>This is </i>La Roca, <i>acknowledged.</i>

552
00:32:10,333 --> 00:32:11,708
This is <i>Majestuoso II, </i>acknowledged.

553
00:32:11,791 --> 00:32:12,666
<i>This is </i>La Proeza, <i>acknowledged.</i>

554
00:32:12,750 --> 00:32:15,125
Did you hear the message
the Harbor Master's Office? Over.

555
00:32:15,208 --> 00:32:18,541
<i>We all heard it, cap. Take it easy. Over.</i>

556
00:32:19,875 --> 00:32:22,416
Hey, Johnny, how are you?

557
00:32:22,958 --> 00:32:26,583
<i>Everything is cool here, cap,</i>
<i>but they've ruined our party.</i>

558
00:32:27,416 --> 00:32:29,333
<i>If it doesn't last long, head over here.</i>

559
00:32:29,416 --> 00:32:32,458
<i>We brought a case of beers,</i>
<i>I'm right next to Marlon. Over.</i>

560
00:32:34,083 --> 00:32:35,208
We're close, then.

561
00:32:36,041 --> 00:32:37,916
See you in a bit. Over and out.

562
00:32:59,083 --> 00:33:01,125
Are they still saying
the same thing in Miami?

563
00:33:01,208 --> 00:33:04,666
Yes, but the sea temperature
is 6 degrees above normal.

564
00:33:05,166 --> 00:33:07,000
And the hurricane keeps intensifying.

565
00:33:07,708 --> 00:33:09,208
You know what that means.

566
00:33:15,250 --> 00:33:17,875
Hurry, we need
to contact the President's Office.

567
00:33:17,958 --> 00:33:20,583
Call a press conference
and gather all the data.

568
00:33:20,666 --> 00:33:23,583
We have to let them know
as soon as possible so they can prepare.

569
00:33:33,625 --> 00:33:35,458
Here! I brought these.

570
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:37,375
Where are you going?

571
00:33:37,458 --> 00:33:38,291
Wirpul.

572
00:34:11,375 --> 00:34:12,458
Are you okay?

573
00:34:12,541 --> 00:34:14,250
I told you this was going to get shitty!

574
00:34:14,333 --> 00:34:16,833
Go aft and nail the fenders.

575
00:34:16,916 --> 00:34:17,791
Fenders?

576
00:34:17,875 --> 00:34:19,416
Which ones are the nails?

577
00:34:19,500 --> 00:34:21,416
Hey, goddamn it, I'm talking to you!

578
00:34:21,500 --> 00:34:23,000
Tie the line to the bitt!

579
00:34:23,083 --> 00:34:24,000
What the fuck is a bitt?

580
00:34:24,083 --> 00:34:25,416
Why don't you know shit?

581
00:34:25,500 --> 00:34:28,375
-Well, I don't know anything!
-A bitt is a cleat, fuck!

582
00:34:28,458 --> 00:34:30,750
You can't even tie down
a damn fender, asshole!

583
00:34:30,833 --> 00:34:32,958
You don't know what a fender is!
You don't know shit!

584
00:34:33,041 --> 00:34:36,208
Next time, bring someone
who can take your bullshit!

585
00:34:38,541 --> 00:34:39,541
Wirpul!

586
00:34:40,500 --> 00:34:43,875
You tied it wrong! Get a knife!

587
00:34:47,708 --> 00:34:49,125
Where's a fucking knife?

588
00:34:49,208 --> 00:34:50,333
In the drawer!

589
00:34:56,166 --> 00:34:57,083
Hurry up!

590
00:34:58,500 --> 00:34:59,458
Hurry up!

591
00:34:59,541 --> 00:35:02,083
-If I cut it, the dinghy will go!
-Cut it!

592
00:35:14,166 --> 00:35:15,458
<i>Watch out, there are two sailboats adrift.</i>

593
00:35:15,541 --> 00:35:18,333
<i>Two sailboats on your side, watch out!</i>

594
00:35:18,416 --> 00:35:21,625
La Princesa <i>is adrift.</i>
<i>I repeat, </i>La Princesa <i>is adrift!</i>

595
00:35:21,708 --> 00:35:23,291
See? What did you get us into?

596
00:35:23,375 --> 00:35:24,500
I told you to leave!

597
00:35:24,583 --> 00:35:26,083
And how am I supposed to leave
without the dinghy?

598
00:35:26,166 --> 00:35:29,833
You tied it up wrong, you idiot!
I almost lost my hand because of you!

599
00:35:29,916 --> 00:35:31,041
-My fault?
-Yes!

600
00:35:31,125 --> 00:35:32,666
You can't take care of yourself!

601
00:35:32,750 --> 00:35:34,541
That's why your mom asked me
to come help you!

602
00:35:34,625 --> 00:35:36,875
You're not a damn captain!

603
00:35:36,958 --> 00:35:38,208
Get off this damn boat!

604
00:35:38,291 --> 00:35:39,250
Stop talking shit!

605
00:35:39,333 --> 00:35:40,833
-Get off, asshole!
-What, asshole?

606
00:35:40,916 --> 00:35:41,791
I'm done with you!

607
00:35:41,875 --> 00:35:44,750
I'm fucking sick of you!
You and your fucking dog!

608
00:35:48,166 --> 00:35:49,166
Fucking hell!

609
00:35:49,250 --> 00:35:50,208
What was that?

610
00:35:50,708 --> 00:35:51,541
Wirpul!

611
00:35:52,166 --> 00:35:53,208
What was that?

612
00:35:56,083 --> 00:35:57,875
One of the lines came loose!

613
00:36:03,333 --> 00:36:04,458
What are you doing?

614
00:36:04,541 --> 00:36:07,666
Slack the lines. If we break loose,
the hurricane will drag us out of the bay.

615
00:36:13,708 --> 00:36:15,291
<i>This is a message</i>
<i>from the Harbor Master's Office.</i>

616
00:36:15,375 --> 00:36:16,208
You're not as stupid as I thought!

617
00:36:16,291 --> 00:36:17,708
<i>All boat skippers and captains</i>

618
00:36:17,791 --> 00:36:20,833
<i>are hereby notified that Hurricane Otis</i>
<i>has reached Category 5,</i>

619
00:36:20,916 --> 00:36:23,041
<i>with wind gusts of up to 186 mph.</i>

620
00:36:23,125 --> 00:36:24,958
Didn't you say that was impossible?

621
00:36:25,041 --> 00:36:26,750
<i>-Exercise extreme caution.</i>
-Hey!

622
00:36:26,833 --> 00:36:28,833
Come help us here at… What's it called?

623
00:36:28,916 --> 00:36:30,458
<i>Majestuoso II, Majestuoso II.</i>

624
00:36:30,541 --> 00:36:32,875
<i>El Majestuoso II!</i>
We need help on <i>Majestuoso II!</i>

625
00:36:36,916 --> 00:36:37,833
You're forcing it!

626
00:36:37,916 --> 00:36:40,583
I'm not forcing it!
I know what I'm doing! Fuck!

627
00:36:43,083 --> 00:36:43,916
What?

628
00:36:47,333 --> 00:36:49,125
-No, no!
-What?

629
00:36:49,208 --> 00:36:51,416
What did I tell you, asshole?
You fucked it up!

630
00:36:52,541 --> 00:36:53,583
Oh, shit!

631
00:36:59,750 --> 00:37:00,583
See?

632
00:37:01,083 --> 00:37:02,041
See? It's burnt out!

633
00:37:02,833 --> 00:37:03,791
Can you fix it?

634
00:37:03,875 --> 00:37:06,666
No! It's already fucked up,
I'm telling you!

635
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:09,208
The other one still works!

636
00:37:09,291 --> 00:37:11,333
We can try to make it
to shore with that one!

637
00:37:11,416 --> 00:37:15,916
No, no! With just one, we're just going
to go around in circles. We can't…

638
00:37:18,625 --> 00:37:19,458
No.

639
00:37:28,166 --> 00:37:29,000
No!

640
00:37:55,500 --> 00:37:58,916
Fuck all this! I don't give a fuck
that you're the captain!

641
00:37:59,000 --> 00:38:01,916
I'm telling you, we're jumping
and making it to the fucking shore!

642
00:38:04,125 --> 00:38:06,625
-You're fucking crazy!
-What?

643
00:38:06,708 --> 00:38:07,916
It's not even a mile!

644
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:10,333
We can't even see the shore, Candi!
We can't see it!

645
00:38:10,416 --> 00:38:12,666
The loose boats are going to crush us!

646
00:38:12,750 --> 00:38:14,333
Even if we make it to shore,

647
00:38:14,416 --> 00:38:16,625
the waves will smash us
against the fucking rocks!

648
00:38:16,708 --> 00:38:19,500
Well, then, what the hell
are we supposed to do?

649
00:38:20,500 --> 00:38:22,333
Staying here is the safest bet.

650
00:38:22,416 --> 00:38:24,166
Yeah, sure! So safe!
Like this is some fucking bunker!

651
00:38:24,250 --> 00:38:25,458
I feel safer, asshole!

652
00:38:25,541 --> 00:38:27,708
Take a look,
and tell me if you can see the shore!

653
00:38:27,791 --> 00:38:29,291
Do you see it?

654
00:38:34,833 --> 00:38:36,666
You're still holding a grudge
about the eye, aren't you?

655
00:38:36,750 --> 00:38:37,875
What?

656
00:38:37,958 --> 00:38:40,333
Even if you deny it,
you still think it was my fault.

657
00:38:40,416 --> 00:38:42,791
What are you talking about?
That was 20 years ago!

658
00:38:42,875 --> 00:38:44,375
And when the hell are you going
to let it go?

659
00:38:44,458 --> 00:38:47,500
-I already let it go, bastard!
-It doesn't look like it, asshole!

660
00:38:55,083 --> 00:38:56,666
Those lines aren't going to hold!

661
00:38:58,083 --> 00:39:01,083
We have to jump!
Take a chance to make it to shore!

662
00:39:03,583 --> 00:39:04,875
I can't leave my boat.

663
00:39:04,958 --> 00:39:06,750
It's not your fucking boat, get it!

664
00:39:07,541 --> 00:39:10,166
If the fucking owner were here,
he'd have jumped already!

665
00:39:13,708 --> 00:39:14,958
It's a boat, Wirpul.

666
00:39:17,166 --> 00:39:19,083
Is it worth more than your life?

667
00:39:19,625 --> 00:39:20,583
Than our lives?

668
00:39:28,583 --> 00:39:29,791
What are you doing?

669
00:39:34,458 --> 00:39:35,375
Luck?

670
00:39:36,125 --> 00:39:39,666
Man, luck is when opportunity
and preparation come together.

671
00:39:40,833 --> 00:39:43,833
I've got 130 years
of luck behind me, you bastard.

672
00:39:43,916 --> 00:39:45,083
Talk to me, Wirpul.

673
00:39:46,208 --> 00:39:49,083
The hurricane hit even harder!
The boat isn't going to hold up!

674
00:39:49,166 --> 00:39:50,291
All the lines are loose!

675
00:39:50,375 --> 00:39:52,625
Come on, calm down, man. What's going on?

676
00:39:52,708 --> 00:39:55,458
<i>The hurricane hit even harder, boss!</i>

677
00:39:55,541 --> 00:39:58,916
Come on, it's just your nerves, Wirpul.
I'm sure it's not that bad.

678
00:40:04,625 --> 00:40:07,208
No, there are lots of boats
and sailboats adrift.

679
00:40:07,291 --> 00:40:08,958
If they hit us, we're going to sink.

680
00:40:09,041 --> 00:40:13,250
<i>No, under no circumstances should you</i>
<i>abandon the boat, you bastard.</i>

681
00:40:13,333 --> 00:40:15,375
But it's really dangerous, boss.

682
00:40:17,625 --> 00:40:18,791
Come on, listen to me,

683
00:40:18,875 --> 00:40:20,958
untie the other boats
that are next to you

684
00:40:21,041 --> 00:40:23,041
<i>so they drift away and won't hit you.</i>

685
00:40:23,125 --> 00:40:25,541
But the other boats
aren't that close, boss.

686
00:40:25,625 --> 00:40:27,125
<i>So, what the fuck is the problem?</i>

687
00:40:27,208 --> 00:40:29,125
They're not close enough for us
to go over and untie them,

688
00:40:29,208 --> 00:40:32,041
but they're close enough to crash into us
if they break loose.

689
00:40:32,125 --> 00:40:34,125
Besides, I don't feel right
doing that, boss.

690
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:37,625
Don't be ridiculous, Wirpul.

691
00:40:37,708 --> 00:40:39,750
Dude, if you don't do it,
someone else will.

692
00:40:39,833 --> 00:40:41,916
Save your job,
let them all go to hell, man.

693
00:40:43,625 --> 00:40:44,458
Yes, boss.

694
00:40:45,250 --> 00:40:46,666
<i>That's it, fucker.</i>

695
00:40:46,750 --> 00:40:49,875
<i>Hell, yeah, Wirpul.</i>
<i>Things will calm down in a minute.</i>

696
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:57,208
This asshole's right. We'd better hurry
before the others beat us to it.

697
00:40:57,291 --> 00:41:00,291
Didn't you hear? It's impossible
to swim to another boat.

698
00:41:00,375 --> 00:41:01,500
Fuck! I'm out of here!

699
00:41:01,583 --> 00:41:03,208
-Where are you going?
-The fuck out of here!

700
00:41:03,291 --> 00:41:05,416
-I'm going to save myself!
-Candi!

701
00:41:06,541 --> 00:41:09,666
You're going to drown
before you reach another yacht.

702
00:41:11,375 --> 00:41:12,458
I'll save myself!

703
00:41:12,541 --> 00:41:14,666
I'm not letting you kill anyone!

704
00:41:15,166 --> 00:41:17,208
Better they cry
at their house than at mine!

705
00:41:17,291 --> 00:41:18,750
You'll kill yourself, asshole!

706
00:41:18,833 --> 00:41:20,541
The eye debt gets paid off today!

707
00:41:20,625 --> 00:41:23,125
We're even! I don't give a damn
about the eye accident!

708
00:41:23,208 --> 00:41:24,333
Hell, no!

709
00:41:27,208 --> 00:41:29,000
This will even the score, man.

710
00:41:29,083 --> 00:41:32,208
We're never going to be okay, Candi,
don't you get it?

711
00:41:32,750 --> 00:41:33,750
We're not family!

712
00:41:34,500 --> 00:41:37,750
We're just another piece of the house
your dad built! That's all!

713
00:41:42,791 --> 00:41:43,750
Don't say that.

714
00:41:47,791 --> 00:41:48,791
I'm not like you.

715
00:41:49,708 --> 00:41:51,916
I don't bring others down to survive.

716
00:41:52,625 --> 00:41:54,583
Today we're not going
to bring anyone down.

717
00:41:54,666 --> 00:41:57,208
Not while I'm the captain, do you get it?

718
00:42:31,208 --> 00:42:33,500
You think it's easy
when your dad just shows up

719
00:42:33,583 --> 00:42:35,375
with a new lady and his mini-me?

720
00:42:36,833 --> 00:42:39,125
I mean, a ton of people do it, right?

721
00:42:39,916 --> 00:42:42,791
But who's so brazen as to go
build a house right next to theirs?

722
00:42:42,875 --> 00:42:45,083
I don't look like him, man. Move.

723
00:42:45,166 --> 00:42:47,041
Oh, yeah. You've got the same face!

724
00:42:48,541 --> 00:42:49,791
And he did love you.

725
00:42:50,958 --> 00:42:54,291
Yeah, is that why he named me
after his washing machine?

726
