Easy. Easy.

978
01:02:39,541 --> 01:02:40,791
Come here.

979
01:02:45,708 --> 01:02:47,208
Bring him. This way.

980
01:02:47,291 --> 01:02:48,208
This way.

981
01:02:48,708 --> 01:02:49,625
This way.

982
01:02:54,208 --> 01:02:55,125
Let me see.

983
01:02:55,875 --> 01:02:56,750
Oh, boy.

984
01:02:56,833 --> 01:02:58,333
Are there any bandages?

985
01:02:58,416 --> 01:03:00,041
Bandages? It's not my boat.

986
01:03:00,125 --> 01:03:02,291
I got here just like you. Mine sank.

987
01:03:03,041 --> 01:03:05,500
I can help him,
but we need a first-aid kit quickly.

988
01:03:07,041 --> 01:03:08,250
We don't have time.

989
01:03:08,333 --> 01:03:10,083
We have to get out of here.

990
01:03:34,666 --> 01:03:35,500
Yes!

991
01:03:41,750 --> 01:03:43,208
Hey!

992
01:03:43,291 --> 01:03:44,958
-What's your name?
-Huh?

993
01:03:45,041 --> 01:03:46,041
What's your name?

994
01:03:46,125 --> 01:03:47,208
-Candi.
-Candi.

995
01:03:47,291 --> 01:03:49,125
Candi. Candi, you're going to be okay.

996
01:03:49,208 --> 01:03:50,416
There's nothing here.

997
01:03:51,750 --> 01:03:53,291
Find a bottle of alcohol.

998
01:03:57,041 --> 01:03:58,708
A bottle of alcohol, quick!

999
01:04:01,666 --> 01:04:03,708
You're going to be fine, Candi.

1000
01:04:03,791 --> 01:04:05,041
Almost there.

1001
01:04:08,458 --> 01:04:10,750
Help me carry him, let's lay him down.

1002
01:04:19,208 --> 01:04:21,083
That's it. I'm going to press.

1003
01:04:25,708 --> 01:04:27,000
Open the bottle!

1004
01:04:34,625 --> 01:04:37,500
My most expensive wound treatment ever.

1005
01:04:41,666 --> 01:04:42,750
Okay, here I go.

1006
01:04:45,291 --> 01:04:46,958
Hold him!

1007
01:04:49,250 --> 01:04:50,625
Relax, relax, Candi.

1008
01:04:54,333 --> 01:04:56,250
Hey, you're going to be fine.

1009
01:04:56,333 --> 01:04:58,416
I don't have anything to sew him up with.

1010
01:04:58,500 --> 01:05:00,041
Don't touch. Don't touch.

1011
01:05:00,583 --> 01:05:01,458
That's it.

1012
01:05:04,000 --> 01:05:06,125
Yes! Yes, that works.

1013
01:05:07,250 --> 01:05:08,166
Give me that.

1014
01:05:09,125 --> 01:05:10,208
Who's the captain?

1015
01:05:10,750 --> 01:05:11,875
Me. Me, me.

1016
01:05:12,583 --> 01:05:14,375
Whose is he for you? Your sailor?

1017
01:05:16,041 --> 01:05:17,125
He's my brother.

1018
01:05:17,916 --> 01:05:19,291
Well, hold him tight.

1019
01:05:19,916 --> 01:05:20,958
Hold him tight!

1020
01:05:21,916 --> 01:05:22,791
Hold him.

1021
01:05:22,875 --> 01:05:23,750
Ready?

1022
01:05:24,250 --> 01:05:25,708
-Ready?
-No! No, no, no!

1023
01:05:27,291 --> 01:05:28,458
Hold him!

1024
01:05:28,541 --> 01:05:30,500
Relax! Hold him tight! Tight!

1025
01:05:31,541 --> 01:05:33,500
Almost there! Almost there!

1026
01:05:35,041 --> 01:05:36,875
This is the last one, the last one.

1027
01:05:36,958 --> 01:05:40,000
There, there. It's over.

1028
01:05:40,750 --> 01:05:41,625
Hold him.

1029
01:05:42,416 --> 01:05:43,416
Press hard!

1030
01:05:44,041 --> 01:05:44,875
Press here.

1031
01:05:46,333 --> 01:05:47,583
Press here, captain!

1032
01:05:49,166 --> 01:05:52,000
We have to get to shore
before we leave the eye.

1033
01:05:53,250 --> 01:05:54,166
The eye?

1034
01:05:54,833 --> 01:05:56,916
We're in the eye of the hurricane.

1035
01:05:57,000 --> 01:05:58,750
Did you think it was over?

1036
01:06:02,000 --> 01:06:05,458
<i>Hurricane Otis made landfall this morning</i>
<i>on the coast of Guerrero</i>

1037
01:06:05,541 --> 01:06:07,000
<i>and continues as a Category 5.</i>

1038
01:06:07,083 --> 01:06:09,125
<i>What was just a tropical storm</i>
<i>intensified explosively,</i>

1039
01:06:09,208 --> 01:06:10,583
<i>taking authorities…</i>

1040
01:06:10,666 --> 01:06:11,583
Fuck.

1041
01:06:11,666 --> 01:06:14,375
<i>-…and the public by surprise…</i>
-No, come on, man.

1042
01:06:14,458 --> 01:06:16,958
It wasn't your fault,
it was those fucking guys' fault.

1043
01:06:17,625 --> 01:06:18,500
Come on.

1044
01:06:22,208 --> 01:06:23,083
Hi, Dad.

1045
01:06:23,833 --> 01:06:27,041
<i>I'm watching the news, Nico.</i>
<i>Do you know anything about the yacht?</i>

1046
01:06:27,125 --> 01:06:30,083
Yeah, I have to tell you something, but…

1047
01:06:30,166 --> 01:06:32,458
<i>-What?</i>
-Please don't get mad.

1048
01:06:32,541 --> 01:06:38,291
The marina's boats broke loose,
and it looks like the yacht sank.

1049
01:06:38,958 --> 01:06:40,291
<i>But it was tied up.</i>

1050
01:06:40,375 --> 01:06:42,750
<i>It was at the back of the yacht club.</i>

1051
01:06:42,833 --> 01:06:43,958
No, Dad.

1052
01:06:44,041 --> 01:06:48,458
<i>Fuck, Nicolás!</i>
<i>I can't trust you to do anything right.</i>

1053
01:06:49,666 --> 01:06:53,791
<i>Listen to me, call Mr. Villalobos</i>
<i>and have him come up</i>

1054
01:06:53,875 --> 01:06:56,166
<i>with a figure to appease the families.</i>

1055
01:06:57,833 --> 01:07:00,750
<i>We need to start gathering</i>
<i>the sailors' insurance documents.</i>

1056
01:07:01,458 --> 01:07:05,916
-What? You think someone died?
<i>-Aren't you watching the news?</i>

1057
01:07:06,416 --> 01:07:07,833
<i>I hope none of them died.</i>

1058
01:07:07,916 --> 01:07:08,916
HURRICANE HITS GUERRERO COAST

1059
01:07:09,000 --> 01:07:10,583
How much money do I give them?

1060
01:07:10,666 --> 01:07:12,208
<i>Come on, Nicolás. You fix this!</i>

1061
01:07:12,291 --> 01:07:14,041
<i>-Take responsibility.</i>
-Dad.

1062
01:07:14,125 --> 01:07:17,083
<i>We'll continue to provide updates</i>
<i>as communications are restored…</i>

1063
01:07:17,166 --> 01:07:19,916
<i>-</i>Fuck.
<i>-…and the first rescue teams arrive.</i>

1064
01:07:20,000 --> 01:07:23,250
<i>We stand in solidarity</i>
<i>to the families of Guerrero.</i>

1065
01:07:48,291 --> 01:07:51,958
This is as far as we go!
We have to jump in and swim to shore!

1066
01:07:53,833 --> 01:07:54,791
We're so close!

1067
01:08:02,791 --> 01:08:04,333
See you on shore!

1068
01:08:13,291 --> 01:08:15,958
Quickly! Let's go there!
That way! Let's go!

1069
01:08:16,041 --> 01:08:17,916
You said you were my brother, right?

1070
01:08:18,000 --> 01:08:19,000
Candi, focus!

1071
01:08:20,041 --> 01:08:21,083
We have to jump!

1072
01:08:21,625 --> 01:08:22,833
Jump now!

1073
01:08:22,916 --> 01:08:24,541
If we jump, we'll drown.

1074
01:08:24,625 --> 01:08:26,416
No one is going to drown!

1075
01:08:26,500 --> 01:08:27,500
We jump on three!

1076
01:08:28,083 --> 01:08:29,916
-One! Two!
-No, wait, wait.

1077
01:08:31,333 --> 01:08:33,125
Do we jump on "one, two, three"?

1078
01:08:33,208 --> 01:08:35,375
Or do we jump
on "one, two, three, and jump"?

1079
01:08:35,458 --> 01:08:36,333
What?

1080
01:08:36,416 --> 01:08:37,875
Three, and then we jump.

1081
01:08:37,958 --> 01:08:39,500
One, two, three!

1082
01:08:39,583 --> 01:08:41,000
We jump!

1083
01:08:41,500 --> 01:08:43,541
That's what I said! We jump on one…

1084
01:08:43,625 --> 01:08:46,416
That's what I said! On three!
One, two, three!

1085
01:08:46,500 --> 01:08:47,416
One!

1086
01:08:48,750 --> 01:08:49,625
Two!

1087
01:08:50,541 --> 01:08:51,458
Three!

1088
01:09:03,875 --> 01:09:04,833
No! Candi!

1089
01:09:05,958 --> 01:09:06,791
No!

1090
01:09:06,875 --> 01:09:08,333
What are you doing, you idiot?

1091
01:09:09,583 --> 01:09:10,458
Jump!

1092
01:09:10,958 --> 01:09:11,916
Jump!

1093
01:09:14,708 --> 01:09:15,666
Jump!

1094
01:09:20,458 --> 01:09:21,333
Candi!

1095
01:09:23,958 --> 01:09:26,000
Candi! No, no!

1096
01:09:26,083 --> 01:09:28,208
No, no!

1097
01:09:28,708 --> 01:09:29,916
No, no! Candi!

1098
01:10:17,416 --> 01:10:19,791
I've got you. I've got you.

1099
01:10:28,500 --> 01:10:29,625
Here, you're safe.

1100
01:10:39,541 --> 01:10:42,541
Let's go! We have to get out of here!

1101
01:10:50,916 --> 01:10:52,583
You have to let him go.

1102
01:10:53,625 --> 01:10:54,666
Captain!

1103
01:10:58,458 --> 01:10:59,708
I'm so sorry.

1104
01:11:01,375 --> 01:11:04,916
But I have to get back to my post.
Are you going to be okay?

1105
01:11:08,000 --> 01:11:09,500
Are you going to be okay?

1106
01:11:59,083 --> 01:11:59,916
Chayo.

1107
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:00,958
Chayo.

1108
01:12:01,041 --> 01:12:01,875
Carmen.

1109
01:12:06,541 --> 01:12:07,541
My house, Chayo.

1110
01:12:08,041 --> 01:12:10,291
-My house, Chayo, it was destroyed.
-Are you okay?

1111
01:12:10,375 --> 01:12:13,791
I am, but my house, Chayo.
What am I going to do, Chayo?

1112
01:12:13,875 --> 01:12:14,916
Wait.

1113
01:12:17,791 --> 01:12:19,291
Come, sit down. Come.

1114
01:12:19,375 --> 01:12:20,583
Oh, Chayo.

1115
01:12:20,666 --> 01:12:21,500
Calm down.

1116
01:12:21,583 --> 01:12:25,291
The house, Chayo, the whole roof
came down, everything fell down.

1117
01:12:25,958 --> 01:12:29,125
Chayo, what am I going to do now?
What am I going to do?

1118
01:12:29,208 --> 01:12:30,916
Don't worry, Carmen.

1119
01:12:31,500 --> 01:12:34,541
We can squeeze in here
while we fix your house.

1120
01:12:34,625 --> 01:12:36,416
And where two can eat, four can eat.

1121
01:12:36,500 --> 01:12:38,208
You don't understand, Chayo.

1122
01:12:38,291 --> 01:12:40,833
Enough, Carmen. Let's stop this nonsense.

1123
01:12:41,875 --> 01:12:43,708
We only have each other.

1124
01:12:45,208 --> 01:12:46,250
And our children.

1125
01:12:47,625 --> 01:12:50,500
I have a huge debt I have to pay, Chayo.

1126
01:12:51,250 --> 01:12:52,875
I don't have anything else.

1127
01:12:52,958 --> 01:12:55,958
That bastard Chevo
didn't leave me anything else.

1128
01:12:56,041 --> 01:12:58,583
That bastard died
and just left me his debt.

1129
01:12:58,666 --> 01:13:00,208
He left it to both of us.

1130
01:13:02,375 --> 01:13:04,000
And to the kids.

1131
01:13:05,041 --> 01:13:05,958
Oh, Chayo.

1132
01:13:06,041 --> 01:13:07,333
That's enough, Carmen.

1133
01:13:07,416 --> 01:13:10,125
Let's stop this fighting, please.

1134
01:13:10,625 --> 01:13:11,541
Chayo.

1135
01:13:14,291 --> 01:13:15,416
Forgive me.

1136
01:13:16,750 --> 01:13:18,041
Oh, Carmen.

1137
01:13:30,750 --> 01:13:32,750
It looks like it's finally waning.

1138
01:13:33,958 --> 01:13:35,583
We have to go look for the boys.

1139
01:13:35,666 --> 01:13:36,500
Let's go.

1140
01:13:37,375 --> 01:13:38,250
Honey.

1141
01:13:39,583 --> 01:13:40,541
Oh, honey.

1142
01:13:44,666 --> 01:13:45,708
Let's go, Chayo.

1143
01:13:46,833 --> 01:13:47,833
Let's go, Mochis.

1144
01:13:59,000 --> 01:13:59,833
Hey!

1145
01:14:00,958 --> 01:14:01,916
Are you okay?

1146
01:14:03,916 --> 01:14:04,750
Hey!

1147
01:14:05,625 --> 01:14:06,458
Hey!

1148
01:14:07,208 --> 01:14:08,208
Do you need help?

1149
01:14:09,208 --> 01:14:10,666
Come here, are you hurt?

1150
01:14:13,791 --> 01:14:14,791
Come on. Come on.

1151
01:14:22,833 --> 01:14:23,875
Don't move.

1152
01:14:53,041 --> 01:14:55,750
Help me get this off! Please, someone!

1153
01:15:05,333 --> 01:15:08,250
No, no. Don't touch it.
You'll get infected.

1154
01:15:09,333 --> 01:15:10,208
Let me do it.

1155
01:15:10,708 --> 01:15:13,166
Here, I didn't need to use your money.

1156
01:15:17,291 --> 01:15:19,125
-Bite down a little.
-No, no.

1157
01:15:19,208 --> 01:15:20,791
Breathe, breathe, breathe.

1158
01:15:22,666 --> 01:15:24,916
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

1159
01:15:35,625 --> 01:15:36,500
Smell it.

1160
01:15:37,125 --> 01:15:39,083
Smell it. It'll keep you awake.

1161
01:15:39,583 --> 01:15:41,583
No, no, it's not for you to drink.

1162
01:15:42,166 --> 01:15:43,250
Where are they?

1163
01:15:54,833 --> 01:15:56,333
Please help me!

1164
01:16:18,541 --> 01:16:19,541
Come.

1165
01:16:24,125 --> 01:16:25,125
Calm down.

1166
01:16:31,666 --> 01:16:33,125
My brother is gone.

1167
01:16:43,041 --> 01:16:43,916
Why?

1168
01:16:45,916 --> 01:16:46,916
No, I don't know.

1169
01:16:49,833 --> 01:16:51,791
We didn't have anything
before this either.

1170
01:16:56,583 --> 01:16:58,583
I have to keep looking for people.

1171
01:16:59,750 --> 01:17:01,000
I have to help them.

1172
01:17:01,541 --> 01:17:03,458
Do you know where your house is?

1173
01:17:03,541 --> 01:17:06,500
I'm looking for my daughter!
She's 8 years old!

1174
01:19:53,958 --> 01:19:55,416
Thirty-seven-year-old woman, head injury.

1175
01:19:55,500 --> 01:19:56,791
PARAMEDIC

1176
01:19:58,208 --> 01:19:59,500
Gauze, please. Gauze.

1177
01:20:00,041 --> 01:20:01,833
Please, wait in reception.

1178
01:20:01,916 --> 01:20:02,916
This way, please.

1179
01:20:10,083 --> 01:20:12,541
Here, check him thoroughly.
Twice if necessary.

1180
01:20:12,625 --> 01:20:14,083
Yes, of course.

1181
01:20:15,916 --> 01:20:17,541
Sir, this way, please.

1182
01:20:17,625 --> 01:20:18,666
With my partner.

1183
01:20:18,750 --> 01:20:19,583
Thank you.

1184
01:20:26,875 --> 01:20:28,291
An ORS, ma'am. An ORS.

1185
01:20:29,583 --> 01:20:30,500
Lemonade!

1186
01:20:31,000 --> 01:20:32,000
Lemonade!

1187
01:20:33,625 --> 01:20:34,625
That way.

1188
01:20:37,041 --> 01:20:39,875
This line is only for locating children.

1189
01:20:40,833 --> 01:20:41,666
PLAZA GALERÍAS

1190
01:20:41,750 --> 01:20:43,541
Paramedic! Paramedic!

1191
01:20:43,625 --> 01:20:47,791
People who have already been treated,
please leave the premises.

1192
01:21:00,750 --> 01:21:03,791
Sure. First, lend it to me for…

1193
01:21:03,875 --> 01:21:06,000
He was my brother,
you're not doing anything!

1194
01:21:06,083 --> 01:21:07,250
What's your name, honey?

1195
01:21:07,333 --> 01:21:09,500
Can you tell me your name and surname?

1196
01:21:09,583 --> 01:21:11,250
We are at full capacity.
Please understand.

1197
01:21:11,333 --> 01:21:12,458
-Mochis?
-Understand…

1198
01:21:12,541 --> 01:21:14,458
-Mochis.
-…that the staff are doing what they can.

1199
01:21:14,541 --> 01:21:15,375
Mochis.

1200
01:21:15,875 --> 01:21:16,708
Mochis.

1201
01:21:16,791 --> 01:21:18,333
Mochis, where's my mom?

1202
01:21:19,666 --> 01:21:21,208
-Where's Mom?
-Wirpul!

1203
01:21:22,541 --> 01:21:23,375
Wirpul.

1204
01:21:24,875 --> 01:21:25,791
Mom?

1205
01:21:26,458 --> 01:21:27,375
Wirpul.

1206
01:21:38,208 --> 01:21:39,083
Honey!

1207
01:21:40,916 --> 01:21:42,083
Wirpul!

1208
01:21:42,958 --> 01:21:44,708
Wirpul.

1209
01:21:45,708 --> 01:21:47,708
My boy.

1210
01:21:49,333 --> 01:21:51,250
I knew you were okay.

1211
01:21:52,250 --> 01:21:53,083
Mom.

1212
01:21:53,958 --> 01:21:55,125
Mom.

1213
01:22:00,000 --> 01:22:03,958
I knew you were okay, my love.
My heart told me so.

1214
01:22:05,291 --> 01:22:08,125
Oh, you're okay!
You're okay! Where's Candi?

1215
01:22:09,000 --> 01:22:10,166
Where's Candi?

1216
01:22:10,250 --> 01:22:11,250
Where's Candi?

1217
01:22:16,333 --> 01:22:18,416
<i>Initial reports continue to come in</i>

1218
01:22:18,500 --> 01:22:21,250
<i>following Hurricane Otis's passage</i>
<i>through Guerrero.</i>

1219
01:22:21,333 --> 01:22:24,833
<i>Overnight, the storm surprised everyone</i>
<i>with its rapid intensification</i>

1220
01:22:24,916 --> 01:22:27,916
<i>and the force</i>
<i>with which it struck the coastal area.</i>

1221
01:22:28,000 --> 01:22:31,208
<i>There is still no clarity</i>
<i>about what is happening in Acapulco.</i>

1222
01:22:31,291 --> 01:22:32,750
<i>Communications remain down,</i>

1223
01:22:32,833 --> 01:22:36,708
<i>and only a few sporadic messages</i>
<i>have managed to get out of the zone.</i>

1224
01:22:36,791 --> 01:22:39,791
<i>The federal government</i>
<i>has activated emergency protocols.</i>

1225
01:22:39,875 --> 01:22:42,791
<i>From what we know so far,</i>
<i>the outlying neighborhoods of Acapulco,</i>

1226
01:22:42,875 --> 01:22:45,833
<i>the poorest not only in Guerrero</i>
<i>but in the entire country,</i>

1227
01:22:45,916 --> 01:22:49,041
<i>have been terribly affected</i>
<i>by the hurricane.</i>

1228
01:22:50,458 --> 01:22:52,125
<i>There's no electricity or drinking water,</i>
<i>and shortages begin…</i>

1229
01:22:52,208 --> 01:22:53,375
Are you okay, dude?

1230
01:22:53,458 --> 01:22:55,416
<i>…to be felt in every corner of the city.</i>

1231
01:22:55,500 --> 01:22:58,583
Dude, can you ask your dad
for some money or…?

1232
01:22:58,666 --> 01:23:01,083
<i>The next few hours</i>
<i>will be decisive in determining…</i>

1233
01:23:01,166 --> 01:23:02,250
Come on, dude.

1234
01:23:02,750 --> 01:23:05,750
You're a swan, Nicolás.
Take it easy, buddy.

1235
01:23:05,833 --> 01:23:08,583
<i>Sources at the hotels have begun</i>
<i>sharing the first images</i>

1236
01:23:08,666 --> 01:23:11,500
<i>showing devastated streets,</i>
<i>torn-off roofs, and buildings…</i>

1237
01:23:11,583 --> 01:23:14,916
Wirpul, how are you, brother?

1238
01:23:15,000 --> 01:23:19,041
<i>Some tourists had to take shelter</i>
<i>elsewhere and improvise barricades.</i>

1239
01:23:19,125 --> 01:23:22,250
<i>We have a firsthand account</i>
<i>from an affected tourist. We're with you.</i>

1240
01:23:22,333 --> 01:23:23,250
Fuck.

1241
01:23:24,833 --> 01:23:26,375
<i>I'd never been in my life…</i>

1242
01:23:26,458 --> 01:23:30,500
I'm so sorry, man,
I don't know what to say.

1243
01:23:33,083 --> 01:23:34,208
I'm here for you, okay?

1244
01:23:34,291 --> 01:23:36,875
<i>This is the most terrifying thing,</i>
<i>honestly.</i>

1245
01:23:52,333 --> 01:23:53,833
-It's nice to see you.
-Thanks.

1246
01:23:53,916 --> 01:23:55,833
Likewise. See you, bye.

1247
01:23:58,208 --> 01:24:01,833
TWO WEEKS LATER
MEXICO CITY

1248
01:24:15,500 --> 01:24:16,375
Wirpul.

1249
01:24:17,375 --> 01:24:18,833
Brother, how are you?

1250
01:24:22,458 --> 01:24:23,916
I'm so sorry, brother.

1251
01:24:25,500 --> 01:24:28,666
How are you? How was the flight?
This is Counselor Villalobos.

1252
01:24:28,750 --> 01:24:30,375
Nice to meet you. How are you?

1253
01:24:30,458 --> 01:24:32,416
Please, sit down.
Make yourself comfortable.

1254
01:24:35,833 --> 01:24:37,875
What? What do you want to drink?

1255
01:24:37,958 --> 01:24:40,291
Order whatever you want, it's on me.

1256
01:24:41,791 --> 01:24:43,333
I'm good, boss. Thanks.

1257
01:24:45,583 --> 01:24:47,041
Well, thanks for coming.

1258
01:24:47,125 --> 01:24:50,500
Things are a total mess here
with all this crap about the…

1259
01:24:50,583 --> 01:24:53,083
The donations and all that crap, you know.

1260
01:24:55,916 --> 01:24:58,500
Again, we're very sorry
about the loss of your sailor.

1261
01:24:58,583 --> 01:24:59,500
My brother.

1262
01:25:00,375 --> 01:25:01,500
His name was Candi.

1263
01:25:02,041 --> 01:25:03,000
Yes, yes, Candi.

1264
01:25:03,083 --> 01:25:03,916
Cándido.

1265
01:25:04,833 --> 01:25:06,041
Yes, yes, Cándido.

1266
01:25:07,541 --> 01:25:12,041
Look, I brought you a little money
to help you out. Just a little something.

1267
01:25:12,125 --> 01:25:16,875
To pay the death benefit for my brother,
who wasn't insured.

1268
01:25:18,250 --> 01:25:19,416
Just like I wasn't.

1269
01:25:21,541 --> 01:25:22,458
Or the boat.

1270
01:25:23,166 --> 01:25:24,916
That's what you mean, right?

1271
01:25:25,000 --> 01:25:27,958
Yes, yes, that's it. Pay the compensation.

1272
01:25:29,083 --> 01:25:30,541
It's my personal money.

1273
01:25:31,041 --> 01:25:32,000
Okay?

1274
01:25:32,875 --> 01:25:34,791
To support you, the family…

1275
01:25:34,875 --> 01:25:36,083
His mom, actually.

1276
01:25:37,458 --> 01:25:38,375
His mother.

1277
01:25:39,333 --> 01:25:40,333
How much is it?

1278
01:25:41,416 --> 01:25:42,291
70K.

1279
01:25:43,875 --> 01:25:47,125
No, I mean, but…
It's just to start, I mean…

1280
01:25:47,208 --> 01:25:49,458
-Only the briefcase is worth 10K.
-Boss.

1281
01:25:51,416 --> 01:25:54,583
Do you think someone's life
is worth 70,000 pesos?

1282
01:25:57,791 --> 01:26:01,083
Someone who worked for you right up
until the last minute before he died.

1283
01:26:03,916 --> 01:26:05,166
You sent us to the slaughterhouse.

1284
01:26:05,250 --> 01:26:06,708
Fuck. Don't say that, Wirpul.

1285
01:26:06,791 --> 01:26:08,625
If I knew it'd be this bad,

1286
01:26:08,708 --> 01:26:10,291
I'd have let the boat sink
and not sent him out--

1287
01:26:10,375 --> 01:26:11,666
I called you, boss.

1288
01:26:13,083 --> 01:26:16,875
I called you to tell you
it was getting bad, to let us come back.

1289
01:26:18,291 --> 01:26:19,125
You preferred…

1290
01:26:20,625 --> 01:26:21,625
saving your boat.

1291
01:26:21,708 --> 01:26:22,666
Come on, Wirpul.

1292
01:26:23,708 --> 01:26:25,000
Don't say that, man.

1293
01:26:25,500 --> 01:26:27,250
-If you're…
-Like family?

1294
01:26:29,666 --> 01:26:31,000
What's my last name?

1295
01:26:35,000 --> 01:26:36,208
I want 300K.

1296
01:26:38,708 --> 01:26:41,500
Three hundred thousand pesos
or I'll tell the Harbor Master's Office

1297
01:26:41,583 --> 01:26:43,625
that you asked me
to release the other boats.

1298
01:26:52,500 --> 01:26:55,541
110K, and you sign a letter
releasing me from all responsibility.

1299
01:26:55,625 --> 01:26:58,875
250K, and I won't tell your dad

1300
01:26:58,958 --> 01:27:02,500
that you kept the money
for the yacht club and the insurance.

1301
01:27:09,291 --> 01:27:12,166
180K. I'll pay for your captain's license.

1302
01:27:12,250 --> 01:27:13,166
Seaman's book.

1303
01:27:13,250 --> 01:27:14,166
That shit.

1304
01:27:23,208 --> 01:27:24,541
Where do I sign?

1305
01:27:29,000 --> 01:27:31,333
Where did you learn
to negotiate like that, huh?

1306
01:27:31,416 --> 01:27:33,333
You're more badass than I thought, man.

1307
01:27:35,000 --> 01:27:36,458
I learned from the best.

1308
01:27:44,291 --> 01:27:46,333
SPACE TRAVELER

1309
01:27:53,625 --> 01:27:54,458
It's done.

1310
01:27:55,958 --> 01:27:57,250
There's your UFO.

1311
01:28:14,875 --> 01:28:16,000
Show your face!

1312
01:28:16,708 --> 01:28:19,166
If you're going to take me,
show your face!

1313
01:28:43,625 --> 01:28:44,500
Wirpul!

1314
01:29:02,875 --> 01:29:04,625
Hey, man, it hurts, asshole!

1315
01:29:05,250 --> 01:29:07,208
It hurts, asshole! Stop!

1316
01:29:07,291 --> 01:29:08,666
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

1317
01:29:08,750 --> 01:29:09,875
Don't be a baby!

1318
01:29:11,583 --> 01:29:13,000
How?

1319
01:29:17,250 --> 01:29:18,125
Asshole.

1320
01:29:19,250 --> 01:29:20,416
It was the aliens.

1321
01:29:27,000 --> 01:29:27,875
Oh, fuck!

1322
01:29:28,375 --> 01:29:29,583
I'll tell you later.

1323
01:29:30,166 --> 01:29:31,041
Listen.

1324
01:29:32,375 --> 01:29:33,250
Take this.

1325
01:29:33,916 --> 01:29:34,833
Take this.

1326
01:29:37,208 --> 01:29:38,083
And this.

1327
01:29:38,958 --> 01:29:40,958
To the first help center you find.

1328
01:29:44,333 --> 01:29:45,458
Where's Candi, son?

1329
01:29:45,541 --> 01:29:48,125
Don't worry, we have a plan.

1330
01:29:57,625 --> 01:29:59,625
Now we just need everything else.

1331
01:30:00,166 --> 01:30:01,500
Give me a break, man.

1332
01:30:02,458 --> 01:30:03,291
Listen.

1333
01:30:07,708 --> 01:30:09,041
Don't you have another song?

1334
01:30:09,625 --> 01:30:10,750
By any chance.

1335
01:30:10,833 --> 01:30:12,250
I don't have space on my phone.

1336
01:30:12,333 --> 01:30:14,500
I just bought you a boat and a phone, man.

1337
01:30:14,583 --> 01:30:16,625
Yeah, but it's a shitty phone,
two for one.

1338
01:30:20,541 --> 01:30:21,625
Are you cheerful?

1339
01:30:22,416 --> 01:30:23,250
Cheerful?

1340
01:30:24,541 --> 01:30:25,916
Well, cheers!

1341
01:30:34,750 --> 01:30:36,875
Want to hear again
about when aliens saved me?

1342
01:30:36,958 --> 01:30:39,541
I felt something grab my ass,
and I started going up.

1343
01:30:39,625 --> 01:30:42,291
No, but it was a fucking huge piece
of wood from that damn boat.

1344
01:30:42,375 --> 01:30:44,291
And then I started to panic,

1345
01:30:44,375 --> 01:30:46,958
and started talking total bullshit, right?

1346
01:30:47,041 --> 01:30:49,083
And then I saw this fucking white light,

1347
01:30:49,166 --> 01:30:50,333
and I'm like, "Shit, I'm dead."

1348
01:30:50,416 --> 01:30:52,375
But no, it was the fucking aliens.

1349
01:30:52,458 --> 01:30:54,750
Then that fucking light
started following me,

1350
01:30:54,833 --> 01:30:56,416
so I swam for it,

1351
01:30:56,500 --> 01:30:57,708
and at some point, it stopped.

1352
01:30:57,791 --> 01:30:59,416
I stopped feeling the fucking current.

1353
01:30:59,500 --> 01:31:01,083
THE LAST FIGURE RELEASED BY THE GOVERNMENT

1354
01:31:01,166 --> 01:31:02,541
FOLLOWING HURRICANE OTIS WAS 68 DEAD.

1355
01:31:02,625 --> 01:31:05,625
32 PEOPLE MISSING, 24 OF THEM AT SEA.

1356
01:31:05,708 --> 01:31:08,625
THERE IS NO OFFICIAL LIST WITH
THE NAMES OF THE DEAD OR THE MISSING.

1357
01:31:08,708 --> 01:31:11,625
HOWEVER, SOME ESTIMATES CALCULATE
MORE THAN TWO HUNDRED DEATHS

1358
01:31:11,708 --> 01:31:14,625
274,000 HOMES AND MORE THAN 600 HOTELS
WERE AFFECTED.

1359
01:31:14,708 --> 01:31:17,625
MORE THAN 800 BOATS DESTROYED.

1360
01:31:17,708 --> 01:31:20,833
16 BILLION DOLLARS IN MATERIAL DAMAGES.

1361
01:31:20,916 --> 01:31:24,791
AND NO UFO SIGHTINGS…

1362
01:31:24,875 --> 01:31:27,166
SO FAR.

1363
01:32:07,000 --> 01:32:09,750
DEDICATED TO THE MEMORY OF THE VICTIMS
AND MISSING PEOPLE OF HURRICANE OTIS.

1364
01:32:09,833 --> 01:32:12,458
MAY THEIR NAMES NEVER FADE WITH TIME,
NOR THEIR STORIES FORGOTTEN.

